</div></div></div><div class="fe-block fe-block-d77d6be1bf3749a60e24"><div class="sqs-block website-component-block sqs-block-website-component sqs-block-html html-block" data-block-css="[&quot;https://definitions.sqspcdn.com/website-component-definition/static-assets/website.components.html/d2a1a69c-95e9-4739-b5f8-14c197d4b62d_1004/website.components.html.styles.css&quot;]" data-block-scripts="[&quot;https://definitions.sqspcdn.com/website-component-definition/static-assets/website.components.html/d2a1a69c-95e9-4739-b5f8-14c197d4b62d_1004/website.components.html.visitor.js&quot;]" data-block-type="1337" data-definition-name="website.components.html" data-sqsp-block="text" data-website-component-id="d77d6be1bf3749a60e24" id="block-d77d6be1bf3749a60e24"><div class="sqs-block-content"><div class="sqs-text-block-container">
  
  <div class="sqs-html-content" data-sqsp-text-block-content><p class="sqsrte-small" style="white-space:pre-wrap;">NEW TO MOTHERCOULD?</p><h2 style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Get to Know Myriam</h2><p class="" style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Myriam Sandler is the creator of Mothercould, a kids activity and family lifestyle community. She shares unique short video tutorials of sensory and food recipes, easy play activities, and educational tools using recycled household items. Born in Venezuela and raised in Miami, FL, the bilingual mother of three offers parents, caretakers and educators simple and accessible play solutions, parenting hacks and more.</p></div>


  
<style id="container-styles">#block-d77d6be1bf3749a60e24 {
    
    --stroke-style: none;--stroke-thickness: 6px;
    
      
      
      
    



  }

  #block-d77d6be1bf3749a60e24 .sqs-html-content {
    
    --tweak-text-block-padding: 6% 6% 6% 6%;
  --tweak-text-block-padding: initial;
}

  .fe-block-d77d6be1bf3749a60e24 {
      mix-blend-mode: var(--tweak-text-block-blend
  );
      border-radius: var(--tweak-text-block-radius);
  }

  
  
.fe-block-d77d6be1bf3749a60e24 {
